# Implementation Plan - Import Facilities from CSV

This plan outlines the steps to add a feature allowing users to import facilities via CSV upload.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> I will be implementing client-side CSV parsing to avoid adding new backend dependencies like `multer`. The data will be sent as a JSON array to a new bulk import endpoint.

## Proposed Changes

### Frontend
#### [MODIFY] [manage-data.html](file:///C:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/manage-data.html) (Assumed filename, will verify)
- Add "Import CSV" button next to "Add Facility".
- Add a hidden file input for CSV selection.
- Add JavaScript to handle file selection, parsing, and sending data to the backend.

### Backend
#### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///C:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/server.js)
- Add `POST /api/facilities/import` endpoint.
- This endpoint will accept an array of facility objects and insert them into the `facilities` table.
- It will handle duplicates (skip or update? Defaulting to skip or basic insert).

## Verification Plan
### Manual Verification
- Create a sample CSV file with valid headers (`name`, `location`, `description`, `boundary_notes`).
- Use the "Import CSV" button to upload the file.
- Verify that the facilities appear in the list.
- Check database content.
